# Eight 64x64 squares in two rows of four on a 256x128 artboard, all simplex fields through the green ramp, so only the field settings differ.
# Top row, left to right: feature size 8 (fine, many small blobs), feature size 32 (coarse, about six dark blobs per square), oct:1 at size 24 (smooth, no fine detail), oct:5 at size 24 (the same blob layout as the oct:1 cell, since the same seed gives the same noise, with extra small-scale grain on top). The simplex cells reach the full dark and light ends of the ramp, with no flat patches.
# Bottom row, left to right: fbm(simplex(24)) (layered, grainy detail, the same layout as the oct:5 cell above), ridged(simplex(24)) (sharp bright creases/ridges instead of soft blobs),
# simplex(24)*worley(24) (a product: darker overall than the plain simplex cells, since multiplying shrinks values), simplex(24 seed:2) (the two seed cells differ from each other in arrangement).
@artboard 256x128
@target fields/shaping.png

rect 64x64 at:32,32 fill:simplex(8 seed:1) -> p.green name:a
rect 64x64 at:96,32 fill:simplex(32 seed:1) -> p.green name:b
rect 64x64 at:160,32 fill:simplex(24 seed:1 oct:1) -> p.green name:c
rect 64x64 at:224,32 fill:simplex(24 seed:1 oct:5) -> p.green name:d
rect 64x64 at:32,96 fill:fbm(simplex(24 seed:1)) -> p.green name:e
rect 64x64 at:96,96 fill:ridged(simplex(24 seed:1)) -> p.green name:f
rect 64x64 at:160,96 fill:simplex(24 seed:1)*worley(24 seed:1) -> p.green name:g
rect 64x64 at:224,96 fill:simplex(24 seed:2) -> p.green name:h
